---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const pageTitle = "About WordCountr — Building the Modern Writing Companion";
const pageDescription = "Learn why we built WordCountr: to replace cluttered, invasive online word counters with a blazing fast, 100% private, client-side writing utility.";
---

<Layout
  title={pageTitle}
  description={pageDescription}
  canonicalSlug="about"
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 bg-white dark:bg-slate-900 p-6 sm:p-12 shadow-xs">
      
      <span class="inline-block rounded-full bg-blue-50 dark:bg-blue-950/40 px-3 py-1 font-mono text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 mb-4 border border-blue-200 dark:border-blue-900">
        Our Mission
      </span>

      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-6">
        About WordCountr
      </h1>

      <div class="prose text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400 space-y-5">
        <p>
          Online word counters should be quiet, lightning-fast utilities that respect your focus and your confidentiality. Instead, the most popular word counters on the web have become billboards plastered with video ads, intrusive tracking scripts, and clunky interfaces that haven't been redesigned in a decade. Even worse: many tools secretly transmit your pasted text to cloud servers where it could be logged or scraped for AI training.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Why We Built WordCountr</h3>
        <p>
          WordCountr was built to fix every flaw in existing counters:
        </p>

        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-xs sm:text-sm">
          <li><strong>100% Client-Side Privacy:</strong> We don't have servers reading your text. Keystrokes are processed locally in your browser RAM.</li>
          <li><strong>Clean, Ad-Free Workspace:</strong> Zero ads around the editor viewport. Zero layout shifts. Instant page load.</li>
          <li><strong>True Offline Capability:</strong> Fully functional PWA that works on airplanes, in subways, or during Wi-Fi blackouts.</li>
          <li><strong>In-Browser File Parsing:</strong> Drag and drop .docx, .pdf, or .txt documents directly into the counter without third-party converters.</li>
          <li><strong>Academic Mode:</strong> The first tool that automatically detects and excludes references and in-text citations for university essay compliance.</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="mt-8 pt-6 border-t border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">
          <h4 class="font-bold text-sm text-slate-900 dark:text-white mb-1">Built for Serious Writers Everywhere</h4>
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-500">
            Whether you are a novelist counting chapters, a student finishing a 500-word essay, or an SEO marketer optimizing keyword density, WordCountr is your precision instrument.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
